---
layout: layouts/piece.njk
title: "The Café — Day's Special Post (1080 × 1350)"
canvasW: "1080px"
canvasH: "1350px"
pageCss: "/assets/css/studio/fb-day-special.css"

# A one-day post, made like the Macho Nachos one (archive/site-src/studio/
# fb-macho-nachos.*): the day's plate and a dessert, a card each. For another
# day, change postDate and the photos; the rest comes from specials.json and
# desserts.json, and the caption (fb-day-special.11tydata.js) reads the same.
postDate: "2026-11-06"
dessert: "Cream Puff"
# The sides as the post says them, when they aren't what specials.json says
# (2026-11-06: carrots; corn until that morning). Leave empty to use the day's.
sidesWords: "mashed potatoes, brown gravy and carrots"
# Another line for the caption only, after the dessert (Mitch 2026-11-05: the
# cookies go in the words, not the picture, so the picture sells the plate).
captionExtra: "New in the dessert fridge: brown butter Triple Chocolate Chip cookies, baked away from gluten, with no food coloring. 2 for $1.75."
# Mitch's photos, cropped to the cards' shape and stripped of camera data.
# The meatloaf is from 2026-10-09: the old specials sign behind it and the
# green beans are blurred, and "carrots" written over them. Without a file,
# that card shows its words only.
platePhoto: "/assets/studio/meatloaf-carrots.jpg"
dessertPhoto: "/assets/studio/cream-puff.jpg"

tags: studio
studioWeekly: true
studioData: ["specials.json", "desserts.json"]
studioTitle: "Day's special and dessert — Facebook post"
studioCategory: "Social"
studioSize: "1080 × 1350 px · portrait feed post"
studioNote: "One day's lunch special with a dessert, like the Macho Nachos post. The plate, price and soup come from that day in specials.json (postDate), the dessert from desserts.json: run npm run desserts after counting them, or the kinds aren't named. The photos are src/assets/studio/meatloaf-carrots.jpg and cream-puff.jpg; without one, that card shows its words only."
studioW: 1080
studioH: 1350
studioOrder: 25
---
{#- One day's plate and a dessert, a row each, photo beside the words.

    THE PLATE is the day in specials.json, found by postDate: its name, its
    price (the day's own or the usual one), the drink, and its sides (or
    sidesWords, when the post says them differently).

    THE DESSERT is desserts.json's: the price, and the kinds Square still
    counts. When it counts none (the file wasn't refreshed after counting),
    no kind is named rather than guessing.

    Every size is set for the ~540px a portrait post shows at on a phone:
    nothing a customer needs is under 24px. -#}
{%- set o = site.opening %}
<div class="canvas mn">

    <header class="mn-head">
        <div class="wordmark wordmark--light wordmark--hero mn-wordmark">
            {% inlineSvg "/assets/thecafe.svg", "", site.name %}
        </div>
        <p class="p-label mn-range">{{ postDate | dayDate("long") }} &middot; {{ site.address.locality }}, {{ site.address.region }}</p>
    </header>

    <div class="mn-body">
        <section class="mn-card">
            {%- if platePhoto | hasAsset %}
            <img class="mn-photo" src="{{ platePhoto }}" alt="">
            {%- endif %}
            <div class="mn-words">
                <p class="p-label mn-label">Lunch special</p>
                <h2 class="p-display mn-name">{{ day.special }}</h2>
                <p class="p-display-italic mn-price">{{ plate.price }}{% if specials.includesDrink %} with a drink{% endif %}</p>
                {%- if plate.sides %}
                <p class="p-body mn-detail">With {{ plate.sides }}</p>
                {%- endif %}
                <p class="p-label mn-served">From 11am</p>
            </div>
        </section>

        {#- The photo on the other side, so the two rows zig-zag. #}
        <section class="mn-card mn-card--flip">
            {%- if dessertPhoto | hasAsset %}
            <img class="mn-photo" src="{{ dessertPhoto }}" alt="">
            {%- endif %}
            <div class="mn-words">
                <p class="p-label mn-label">For dessert</p>
                <h2 class="p-display mn-name">{{ dessert }}</h2>
                <p class="p-display-italic mn-price">{{ sweet.price }} each</p>
                <p class="p-body mn-detail">{% if sweet.kinds %}{{ sweet.kinds | capitalize }}, while{% else %}While{% endif %} they last</p>
            </div>
        </section>
    </div>

    <footer class="mn-foot">
        <p class="p-display mn-foot-call">{{ site.phone }} <span class="dot">&middot;</span> {{ site.social.website }}</p>
        <p class="p-body mn-foot-line">{{ postDate | dayDate("weekday") }} {{ o.opens.time | replace(":00", "") }}{{ o.opens.meridiem }} &ndash; {{ o.closes.time | replace(":00", "") }}{{ o.closes.meridiem }} &middot; {{ site.address.street }}, {{ site.address.locality }}, {{ site.address.region }}</p>
    </footer>

</div>
